Here's another wrinkle. If I use the "manual" method of running the MCMC: `CHMC$run(niter=2000, nburnin=1000)`, I don't see the slowdown.

So that's another work-around. You can read about using $run in the manual <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-mcmc.html#sec:executing-the-mcmc-algorithm>. You would need to manually handle running multiple chains if you want multiple chains.

