Hi Sarah,
That's a good question and I wish I knew more to give you a good answer. nimble does C++ compilation by issuing a system call to "R CMD SHLIB". Whatever that needs (at least a C++ compiler, possibly make or other components to a full tool chain) is what nimble needs. I'm not sure of your Shiny deployment needs. When you install Rtools, do you get options to customize what is installed? I found an R blog article <https://blog.r-project.org/2025/01/28/alternative-toolchains-on-windows/?utm_source=chatgpt.com> on the general topic of Windows Rtools alternatives, although it looks written towards an expert audience.
Does anyone else on the list have knowledge of Rtools components or alternative setups?
Perry

